dirtygarden-by-faemiyah for Debian
----------------------------------

The upstream source has two build modes:
 * the compo mode, which loads its symbols by hand and ends with 32-bit x86
   assembly, to fit in 4 kilobytes (FreeBSD ia32 only);
 * the USE_LD mode, plain C linked normally against SDL and OpenGL.

The package is built in the USE_LD mode (DEB_CFLAGS_MAINT_APPEND in
debian/rules), which is portable: it is built for amd64, i386, armhf, arm64
and riscv64.

The Debian patches move the intro from SDL 1.2 to SDL2, start it in a
resizable window (F toggles fullscreen) and fix the shaders
for strict GLSL compilers.

The rel/ directory of the upstream archive contains the original prebuilt
executables (FreeBSD, Linux, Windows); they are neither used nor installed.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>, reviewed by Nicolas HOUDELOT.

